  "note": "Allowlist for OTRF Security-Datasets JSON-lines exports (flat-timecreated and nxlog-eventtime shapes). Event types without an entry are imported metadata-only (SourceName/Level/Severity/Task/Opcode); unlisted fields are dropped and counted. Content fields (command lines, script blocks, module payloads, registry values, DNS results, service image paths, task XML, WMI consumer text, group memberships, filter conditions, application messages) use the `content` transform: benchmark_sanitize redacts secrets, pseudonymizes identities with the structured-field pseudonyms, masks ATT&CK tokens and truncates explicitly at 16384 bytes. CallTrace, Sysmon RuleName, AccessReason and security descriptors remain absent. message_fields names a parser that extracts fields from the rendered Message when the export carries the event data nowhere else (classic Windows PowerShell; UserData events in the NXLog shape); extracted fields fill only names the record lacks. shape_aliases rename an original field of one record shape to the allowlisted name of the SAME Windows field (verified on the inspected exports). Any operator who adds a field takes responsibility for its release review.",
  "schema_version": 1,
